From 777aec07c585b3ae8a1d8bccc4f4b8165d706134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkraiHL <16268229+DarkraiHL@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:53:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] platform: detect Hopper (SM90) GPUs

DeepInfer's GPU code paths target SM100. On a Hopper GPU the engine
does not start: get_bf16_tflops_limit() raises "unknown GPU type" when
LLMEngine sets up its stats logger, and several pinned kernels are
built for SM100 only. Add the detection that the following commits
build on:

- deep_cluster.hardware: is_sm90() (compute capability 9.0 of device 0,
  read via NVML so no CUDA context is created) and
  nvidia.device_name(). get_bf16_tflops_limit() returns the dense BF16
  peak on SM90: 148 TFLOPS for H20 / H20-3e (matched as a whole model
  name, so H200 is not taken for H20), 989 TFLOPS for other SM90 parts.
- PLATFORM.is_sm90 (False on every non-NVIDIA platform), the switch
  every SM90 path in this series uses, and an empty sm90_ops package
  for the SM90 kernels.
- hc.py: DeepGEMM's mega_mhc is SM100-only, so SM90 uses the existing
  TileKernels mHC path.
- runtime_config: on SM90, NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE defaults to 0 because many
  Hopper systems cannot initialize NVLS (CUDA error 401/802 in
  ncclMcGroupBuildPartitions); setting it in the environment still
  wins. Other platforms keep unsetting it as before.

Every behaviour change is gated on is_sm90; SM100 and Ascend paths are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
