From 16f7e44bfe267bba3f07a1c3b7841f8827546a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkraiHL <16268229+DarkraiHL@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:53:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] build: build the SM90 (Hopper) dependencies from
 build.sh

`DEEPINFER_ACCELERATOR=nvidia ./build.sh` now selects the GPU
architecture to build for (scripts/cuda_arch.sh: DEEPINFER_CUDA_ARCH=
sm90|sm100, detected from the first GPU's compute capability, sm100
when no GPU is visible) and on SM90:

- installs requirements-sm90.txt (humming-kernels 0.1.12, used by the
  default SM90 MoE backend added later in this series) before NCCL is
  re-pinned to 2.32.3, so 2.32.3 stays the only NCCL in the
  environment;
- builds FlashMLA's Hopper kernels from the new submodule
  vendor/FlashMLA-SM90 (ba89a34, the last FlashMLA commit with SM90
  kernels), installed as flash_mla_sm90, instead of the SM100-only
  vendor/FlashMLA.

scripts/build_vendor.sh applies scripts/vendor_patches/<package>/
*.patch and, for NVIDIA builds, <package>/<arch>/*.patch right before
building each package, and reverts them when that build ends (also on
failure), so the submodules stay at their pinned commits:

- FlashMLA-SM90 0001: extends ba89a34's SM90 sparse decode kernel to
  DeepInfer's token-interleaved V4.1 KV caches (V41: 512 x e4m3 +
  16 x ue8m0 per token; V41_FP4: 512 x e2m1 + 32 x e4m3 per token, as
  the extra cache), dequantizing both to bf16 exactly, and renames the
  package to flash_mla_sm90, built with -fvisibility=hidden so it can
  be installed next to the pinned flash_mla.
- DeepSelect sm90/0001: also compile sm_90a, so top-k runs on Hopper.
- DeepSelect sm90/0002: bf16 rows of >= 512K entries (batch <= 6)
  dispatch to a 16-CTA non-portable cluster kernel that H20 cannot
  launch ("cluster misconfiguration", hit by decode top-k with a ~1M
  max_model_len); GPUs before SM100 take the regular kernel.
- DeepEP 0002: RDMA bandwidth / atomics detection queries
  $EP_RDMA_NIC_NAME if set, else mlx5_0 when ibstat lists it (as
  before), else the first CA with an active port (e.g. bonded
  mlx5_bond_* NICs), instead of always querying mlx5_0.

All of these patches apply to SM90 builds only; SM100 and Ascend
builds are unchanged. The patches are listed
in scripts/vendor_patches/README.md and are candidates for the
respective upstream projects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
