From b1f3b7dc2fb1939876ab87daeb76951fda7badcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkraiHL <16268229+DarkraiHL@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:53:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] attention: run V4.1 sparse attention on SM90

The pinned FlashMLA (2e5429f) ships SM100 kernels only. On SM90,
attention_backend.py imports flash_mla_with_kvcache,
flash_mla_sparse_fwd and FlashMLASchedMeta from sm90_ops/flash_mla.py,
which keeps the 2e5429f signatures (its interface code follows
FlashMLA's flash_mla_interface.py; MIT notice in the file) on top of
flash_mla_sm90, built by the previous commit:

- sparse decode: ba89a34's SM90 split-KV kernel extended to the V41
  (SWA / main) and V41_FP4 (compressed extra) KV caches, so DeepInfer's
  cache layout and numerics stay unchanged;
- sparse prefill: ba89a34's SM90 kernel as is.

The fused norm+rope+attn+rope+cast kernel is SM100-only, so
V4AttentionBase uses its existing unfused path on SM90. The input
metadata now takes FlashMLASchedMeta from attention_backend, so it
follows the selected build.

configure_worker_kernels() checks on SM90 that flash_mla_sm90 is
installed (with an error that says how to build it) and rejects
DEEPINFER_BATCH_INVARIANT=1: the SM90 decode kernel always splits the
KV across SMs, and the SM90 routed-expert kernels added later are not
batch invariant either.

examples/offline_inference.py no longer defaults
DEEPINFER_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 on SM90, and the offline decode-PPL tests
are skipped there: their NVIDIA goldens are measured on SM100 with
batch invariance.

Gated on PLATFORM.is_sm90; the SM100 imports are unchanged.
tests/sm90/test_flash_mla_sm90.py checks decode (V41 / V41_FP4 extra
caches, sparse and dense extra indices) and prefill against an fp32
torch reference on caches written by DeepInfer's store_kv_cache, and
that single-key rows reproduce the reference dequantization bit for
bit.

