From c32bf07b461f0c72c2d57bc340ee213f5e79a9b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkraiHL <16268229+DarkraiHL@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:54:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] moe: run MXFP4 routed experts on SM90

DeepInfer runs MXFP4 routed experts through deep_gemm's
fp8_fp4_mega_moe or, on the non-mega EP path,
m_grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm_nt_contiguous with packed FP4 weights; both are
SM100-only, and so is the BF16 mega gate. On SM90, DeepseekMoE now
disables mega MoE and the mega gate (the gate falls back to
moe_topk_gate), keeps DeepEP V2 dispatch / combine with the expanded
psum layout, and replaces the two grouped GEMMs with
sm90_ops.moe.Sm90RoutedExperts, which takes over the packed MXFP4
parameters at construction (the originals are released). Dispatch
produces row-major activation scales for it, and the forward passes a
host-side row-count hint (local tokens x top-k) that is only used to
pick tiles and kernels. EPLB shuffles the per-expert tensors that
Sm90RoutedExperts reports. Expert types other than MXFP4 weights with
FP8 activations raise at init on SM90.

Backends, selected with DEEPINFER_SM90_MOE_BACKEND (registered in
deepinfer/environ.py):

- humming: humming-kernels (PyPI, Apache-2.0, validated with 0.1.12)
  W4A8 indexed GEMM; experts keep the MXFP4 footprint. A small Triton
  kernel turns psum into humming's tile list on device, without a host
  sync, so the forward can be captured in a CUDA graph. humming
  re-rounds 32-groups whose exponent is more than 11 below their
  matrix's maximum; this is counted and logged once at init, and on
  DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash only touches 28 of the 384 MTP w13 matrices.
- triton_fp8: MXFP4 upcast to FP8 with 128x128 power-of-two block
  scales (checked to be exact) and a Triton block-FP8 grouped GEMM
  adapted from SGLang's fused_moe_kernel (v0.5.22, itself derived from
  vLLM; Apache-2.0) on the same tile list. No extra dependency; about
  twice the expert memory.
- hybrid: keeps both weight copies and picks triton_fp8 when the row
  hint is at least DEEPINFER_SM90_MOE_HYBRID_MIN_ROWS (default 4096),
  humming otherwise.
- deepgemm: the same FP8 upcast through DeepGEMM's SM90 grouped FP8
  GEMM; mainly a cross-check.
- auto (default): humming when humming-kernels is installed, otherwise
  triton_fp8 with a warning. A selected backend that is not installed,
  or an FP8 expert copy that does not fit in free memory, fails at init
  with an actionable message.

Gated on PLATFORM.is_sm90; SM100 paths are unchanged.
tests/models/test_sm90_moe.py covers the psum -> tile mapping, the
scale conversion, the exactness of the upcast, backend resolution, and
every backend against a float32 model with poisoned alignment-gap rows
(cosine and relative-norm bounds).

